settings.definition_quote:
In each round, a user $u(t)$ is sampled independently from a distribution $\probuser$ over $[\s{N}]$ (for much of the paper, we assume $\probuser$ is the uniform distribution). The sampled user $u(t)$ pulls an arm $\rho(t)$ from the set $[\s{M}]$ and receives a reward $\fl{R}^{(t)}$, s.t., 
\begin{align}\label{eq:obs}
    \fl{R}^{(t)} = \fl{P}_{u(t)\rho(t)}+\eta^{(t)}
\end{align}
where $\eta^{(t)}$ denotes the additive noise that is added to each observation. We will assume that the noise sequence $\{\eta^{(t)}\}_{t \in [\s{T}]}$ is composed of i.i.d zero-mean sub-Gaussian
random variables with variance proxy at most $\sigma^2>0$.
